A||N||5||Ferrari355||I have a question!||||8||
Z||000000||Ferrari355||01-25-2000||11:07 PM||||Ok, when I was driving my Fiero around in front og our garage when I hit a bump the dome lights under the dash came on and then they would go off. Actually they would sorta fliker and either stay on or go off. Then now when you get in the car they go off and then imediatly come back on once the door is shut. And when your on the outside looking in the window if you press on the drivers door the lights will go off or even when you pull on the handle thing. You basicly have to slam the door real hard for them to go off. So Today when I went outside after I got home from school I was going to start the car and drive it around in front of the garage "i'm only 14" and the thing wouldn't even turn over. Last night when I shut the doors I made sure they were off but I guess they came back on. Do you guys know what is wrong with freaking lights? We were going to jump it to but the jumper cables were in our truck and it was 70 miles away!!!! UGH!!! E-mail me if you know what is wrong. or jsut reply . <A HREF="mailto:AlexB2004@aol.com">AlexB2004@aol.com</A> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||01-25-2000||11:24 PM||||You might have had the same bizarre problem that I had some while ago with my 85 GT. It was ONLY the foot well lights that went on and not anything else? I thought that it was from the previous owners butchery, uh I mean modifications of some wires under the dash. Im trying to remember how I found it now....I believe it was something really weird....I think it had to do with my trunk light, I had stuffed the trunk with luggage and accidently pulled out the trunk light, it had sit in a way that the hot wire was grounding out on the chassis and throught the miracle of wiring sent power to the footlights. To make sure I simply unpluged the trunk light and kept it to see if it happend again. It didn't and I saw that one of the plastic tabs had broken off. New one in no problems since. Until you find out you can simply take out the bulbs so that you don't kill the battery. <P>Good luck! Let us know what happens!<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 01-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ferrari355||01-25-2000||11:29 PM||||This weird. cause when I found the trunk light, itwas unplugged so I plugged it and then the it drained the battery. So I unplugged it, and since then the foot lights are the only ones that come on and it drives me crazy. I dunno, but we are thinking of replacing the dome light switch to see if it is bad. Before we traded our 94 Intrepid ES in once the dome light stayed on and wouldn't go off and it was the switch also. When I figure it out I'll let you know ok. Thanks for the info! ||||reg||4
Z||000003||David Gamache||01-26-2000||12:32 AM||||Check for a worn out pin switch in the doors or in the front or rear bonnet areas. i had a faulty rear pin switch that caused battery problems and a faulty door switch that let interior iights go on and off. with the overhead lamps commimg on look to see if the two lamps in the middle are the ones lighting. if they are, they are connected to the door pins system, so are the floor lamps. If the outer lights on the overhead are comming on the rear screws, in the lamp under  the lens serves as a ground and may be loose. just a few thoughts  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||862M4inCA||01-26-2000||03:30 AM||||Another possibility worth looking into which happened to me once before is to make sure that you don't have a blown coutesy/decklid fuse. I found that if that fuse is blown and you have one of the overhead map lights in the on position that the footwell lights come on, but the map light will not. I'm assuming that the two circuits are connected in some funky fashion that will still provide some power to each other. However if you don't have a blown fuse then I would check for worn door switches.||||reg||1
Z||000005||86SE||01-26-2000||04:30 PM||||I had the same exact problem, first thing I checked was the fuses.  Turned out it was just a fuse, can't remember which one it was......................||||reg||1
